07:42:23.380 --> 07:42:27.260
So we have X minus F divided by S plus one.

07:42:27.260 --> 07:42:29.540
And then we'll leave from this

07:42:29.540 --> 07:42:32.600
to this feature map right here.

07:42:32.600 --> 07:42:34.740
Notice how we still maintain the number of channels,

07:42:34.740 --> 07:42:39.740
but our input feature map has been subsampled.

07:42:39.740 --> 07:42:43.900
For the particular case of max pooling,

07:42:43.900 --> 07:42:45.700
if you want to understand how this works,

07:42:45.700 --> 07:42:48.160
let's say we are at this position.

07:42:48.160 --> 07:42:49.260
Let's take this position.

07:42:49.260 --> 07:42:51.380
Let's take a position where we have some values.

07:42:51.380 --> 07:42:53.660
Notice how as we pick this value,

