07:43:03.080 --> 07:43:04.380
So basically what we're doing is

07:43:04.380 --> 07:43:07.760
we're just simply sliding through the whole image.

07:43:07.760 --> 07:43:11.980
And then for every, since our kennel size is equal to two,

07:43:11.980 --> 07:43:14.920
we have a two by two kennel size here.

07:43:14.920 --> 07:43:17.640
So for every four values,

07:43:18.540 --> 07:43:21.320
we are gonna pick out one to represent them.

07:43:21.320 --> 07:43:24.860
And in this case, this one is the max.

07:43:24.860 --> 07:43:28.400
In some cases, we will instead take the average of this.

07:43:28.400 --> 07:43:30.260
That is known as average pooling.

07:43:30.260 --> 07:43:31.540
But for this max pooling,

07:43:31.540 --> 07:43:35.040
