07:45:44.160 --> 07:45:46.800
We have the relu added and then we have this output.

07:45:46.800 --> 07:45:51.440
So we have the output 26 by 26 by 16.

07:45:51.440 --> 07:45:53.320
Recall number of filters dictates

07:45:53.320 --> 07:45:55.360
the number of channels right here

07:45:55.360 --> 07:45:58.640
and not the filter sizes, the number of filters.

07:45:58.640 --> 07:46:00.520
And then this 26 by 26 is gotten

07:46:00.520 --> 07:46:03.440
by using the same formula we've seen already.

07:46:03.440 --> 07:46:07.640
From here, we have another subsampling.

07:46:07.640 --> 07:46:08.800
We've understood that already

07:46:08.800 --> 07:46:10.800
and then we flatten all this out.

07:46:10.800 --> 07:46:13.080
So after doing the subsampling,

07:46:13.080 --> 07:46:15.480
we have this 13 by 13 by 16.

07:46:15.480 --> 07:46:19.640
When you multiply all this, it should give you 2,704.

07:46:20.800 --> 07:46:22.920
And this is what we call the flatten layer.

07:46:22.920 --> 07:46:25.720
So we pass this to a flatten layer to obtain this.

07:46:25.720 --> 07:46:28.960
Now this takes each and every value we have here

07:46:28.960 --> 07:46:32.840
in our feature map and then just simply places it

07:46:32.840 --> 07:46:37.280
in this one dimensional output right here.

07:46:37.280 --> 07:46:39.200
Then from here, we have the dense layer,

07:46:39.200 --> 07:46:41.360
which we're used to working with already.

07:46:41.360 --> 07:46:45.840
And then we have a thousand neurons in the output.

07:46:45.840 --> 07:46:48.280
And finally, we have 200 neurons.

07:46:48.280 --> 07:46:50.520
In our case, we should have two

07:46:50.520 --> 07:46:55.000
since we're actually predicting whether it's a parasite

07:46:55.000 --> 07:46:58.320
or it's a parasite, so we should just have two.

07:46:58.320 --> 07:47:00.640
Anyways, we understand all this now

07:47:01.920 --> 07:47:04.760
and we should be ready to dive into the code.

07:47:04.760 --> 07:47:06.600
Before moving on to the code,

07:47:06.600 --> 07:47:09.320
let's get to see what the feature maps

07:47:09.320 --> 07:47:13.480
of a trained convolutional neural network looks like.

07:47:13.480 --> 07:47:16.080
As you could see right here from this example

07:47:16.080 --> 07:47:18.080
from the Stanford website,

07:47:19.160 --> 07:47:20.960
we have this car which is passed

07:47:20.960 --> 07:47:23.120
into a convolutional neural network

07:47:23.120 --> 07:47:27.200
and then its output, we have it predicting a car.

07:47:28.760 --> 07:47:30.200
As you can notice,

07:47:30.200 --> 07:47:35.200
this first layers actually serve as filters

07:47:36.560 --> 07:47:40.240
for low level features like the edges.

07:47:40.240 --> 07:47:45.240
So you'll notice that this input or this feature maps

07:47:45.240 --> 07:47:52.240
from the first layers produce visually interpretable outputs.

07:47:53.280 --> 07:47:58.280
Now you will notice also that as we go farther or deeper,

07:47:58.400 --> 07:48:03.320
we have this outputs which are less visually interpretable.

07:48:03.320 --> 07:48:07.240
And the focus more on high level features

07:48:07.240 --> 07:48:09.080
like the car parts,

07:48:09.080 --> 07:48:12.120
which per meters correctly classified

07:48:12.120 --> 07:48:15.560
that this image contains a car.

07:48:16.840 --> 07:48:20.840
And so the first layers are for feature extraction

07:48:20.840 --> 07:48:25.480
and then the last layers are for classification.

07:48:26.320 --> 07:48:29.880
Both subsections actually need each other

07:48:29.880 --> 07:48:32.680
as if you do feature extraction

07:48:32.680 --> 07:48:35.360
and you don't have layers which are able

07:48:35.360 --> 07:48:38.980
to permit us correctly, classify this image,

07:48:38.980 --> 07:48:43.400
then we will not achieve our goal.

07:48:43.400 --> 07:48:45.960
And in the same sense,

07:48:45.960 --> 07:48:48.780
if we have a good classifier,

07:48:48.780 --> 07:48:52.820
but we get this kind of inputs directly,

07:48:54.200 --> 07:48:58.800
where we've not extracted useful features from them yet,

07:48:58.800 --> 07:49:01.760
then our classifier is not gonna perform well.

