08:30:49.100 --> 08:30:53.540
we'll need to find a way to export this model from here.

08:30:53.540 --> 08:30:57.980
And so TensorFlow allows us to save our model.

08:30:57.980 --> 08:31:01.980
Now we'll have to differentiate between a model's

08:31:01.980 --> 08:31:05.100
configuration and a model's weights.

08:31:05.100 --> 08:31:10.060
So a model like this, let's suppose we have a model

08:31:10.060 --> 08:31:11.860
which is defined as such.

08:31:11.860 --> 08:31:15.260
We have the input, which we pass into a count layer

08:31:15.260 --> 08:31:17.660
then we have batch normalization,

08:31:17.660 --> 08:31:21.620
we have pooling for subsampling and then we flatten

08:31:21.620 --> 08:31:23.820
and after flattening, we pass through a dense layer

08:31:23.820 --> 08:31:24.980
and we have our output.

08:31:24.980 --> 08:31:28.060
So suppose we have this small model.

08:31:28.060 --> 08:31:33.060
Now, all the parameters for the creation of this model

08:31:34.700 --> 08:31:37.780
are known as the model's configuration.

08:31:37.780 --> 08:31:39.780
In the model's configuration,

08:31:39.780 --> 08:31:42.820
we may have it that the model for example,

08:31:42.820 --> 08:31:45.460
like in this case here,

08:31:45.460 --> 08:31:49.780
the model starts with a count layer with six filters,

08:31:49.780 --> 08:31:52.380
kind of size three, batch norm and all this.

08:31:52.380 --> 08:31:56.180
So these are our model's configurations,

08:31:56.180 --> 08:31:59.020
but this model's configurations are different

08:31:59.020 --> 08:32:01.020
from the model's weights.

08:32:01.020 --> 08:32:05.540
The model's weights are those filters we have,

08:32:05.540 --> 08:32:08.620
for example, in the case of the conf 2D.

08:32:08.620 --> 08:32:10.820
So we have the model weights

08:32:10.820 --> 08:32:15.220
and the model's configuration.

08:32:15.220 --> 08:32:17.220
And upon summarizing the model,

08:32:17.220 --> 08:32:21.100
we see clearly here that we have this conf 2D

08:32:21.100 --> 08:32:24.860
and then we have this number of parameters.

08:32:24.860 --> 08:32:28.300
And so whenever we want to save a model,

08:32:28.300 --> 08:32:30.300
we have to take into consideration

08:32:30.300 --> 08:32:33.180
this configuration and the weights

08:32:33.180 --> 08:32:36.100
because for this same configuration,

08:32:36.100 --> 08:32:37.660
we could have different weights.

08:32:38.860 --> 08:32:42.060
And so there are actually two main options.

08:32:42.060 --> 08:32:46.180
The first option is to save the full model.

08:32:46.180 --> 08:32:49.740
That is to save the model configuration

08:32:49.740 --> 08:32:51.700
and the model weights.

08:32:51.700 --> 08:32:56.700
Another option will be to save only the model weights.

08:32:56.700 --> 08:32:59.340
So we could save only the model weights.

08:32:59.340 --> 08:33:03.900
Now, this option is used when, for example,

08:33:03.900 --> 08:33:06.940
we don't want to, or we don't even know

08:33:06.940 --> 08:33:09.540
this model configuration upfront.

08:33:09.540 --> 08:33:12.180
So we have used this year,

08:33:12.180 --> 08:33:14.300
we've defined the model's configuration,

08:33:14.300 --> 08:33:16.980
we've trained it, we've got a new weights

08:33:16.980 --> 08:33:19.940
and this is the current model state.

08:33:19.940 --> 08:33:21.820
But if we take this to another environment

08:33:21.820 --> 08:33:26.220
where we don't have this configuration,

08:33:26.220 --> 08:33:30.820
then if we've saved this model's configuration and weights,

08:33:30.820 --> 08:33:35.220
all we need to do is just to load this configuration

08:33:35.220 --> 08:33:39.500
and weights which have been packaged as the full model.

08:33:39.500 --> 08:33:42.420
Now, in another case where we are able

08:33:42.420 --> 08:33:46.860
to get the configuration and all we need is just the weights

08:33:46.860 --> 08:33:51.700
then we'll just save the weights and then reload this weights

08:33:51.700 --> 08:33:54.220
since we already have the configuration.

08:33:54.220 --> 08:33:57.300
Either ways, we'll always need the configuration

08:33:57.300 --> 08:33:59.420
and the weights.

08:33:59.420 --> 08:34:01.700
Nonetheless, it's important to note that

08:34:01.700 --> 08:34:04.720
the most important part of this is actually the weights

08:34:04.720 --> 08:34:08.900
since working with a randomized or randomly initialized

08:34:08.900 --> 08:34:13.700
weights after we've trained our model isn't very useful.

08:34:13.700 --> 08:34:17.460
And sometimes we may take many days to train this model.

08:34:17.460 --> 08:34:21.140
So imagine you've trained your model for like 10 days

08:34:21.140 --> 08:34:23.780
and then you wanna reuse that model

08:34:23.780 --> 08:34:26.500
and the weights have been randomly initialized.

08:34:26.500 --> 08:34:29.020
You find that those 10 days have been wasted

08:34:29.020 --> 08:34:31.940
both time-wise and monetary-wise.

08:34:31.940 --> 08:34:35.420
So you have to ensure that you save your weights properly

08:34:35.420 --> 08:34:37.860
such that you could reuse them.

08:34:37.860 --> 08:34:40.700
And then the great thing with TensorFlow is

08:34:40.700 --> 08:34:43.700
you could also continue training from the state.

08:34:43.700 --> 08:34:47.440
So this means that at this point where we've gotten

08:34:47.440 --> 08:34:52.440
this model's performance year where we have 94%,

08:34:52.820 --> 08:34:55.960
we could keep training from year so that we could get

08:34:55.960 --> 08:34:59.420
even to say 99%.

08:34:59.420 --> 08:35:04.060
So you have to ensure that your saving is done properly.

