and then comes this way, we have this right here.

09:53:13.120 --> 09:53:15.180
So if we have this kind of ROC plot,

09:53:15.180 --> 09:53:19.140
then we will be able to pick out

09:53:19.140 --> 09:53:24.140
this threshold right here, 0.0, say X.

09:53:24.140 --> 09:53:26.640
We'll be able to pick this threshold

09:53:26.640 --> 09:53:30.320
because at this threshold, for this threshold,

09:53:30.320 --> 09:53:33.000
at this point, the true positive rate

09:53:33.000 --> 09:53:35.560
is at its highest value, that is of one.

09:53:35.560 --> 09:53:37.240
And then the false positive rate

09:53:37.240 --> 09:53:40.560
is at its lowest possible value, that is of zero.

09:53:40.560 --> 09:53:43.000
So here we have one and then zero.

09:53:43.000 --> 09:53:44.960
So here we go, we have this

09:53:44.960 --> 09:53:47.160
and then we pick out the threshold.

09:53:47.160 --> 09:53:51.120
Now this value of X could be five, could be four, whatever.

09:53:51.120 --> 09:53:54.740
So we have a zero point, whatever value

09:53:54.740 --> 09:53:56.640
will lead us to this.

09:53:57.800 --> 09:53:59.920
Nonetheless, many times we wouldn't have

09:53:59.920 --> 09:54:00.760
this kind of plots.

09:54:00.760 --> 09:54:04.880
So we will do it plus, which will look like this,

09:54:05.920 --> 09:54:08.600
this and so on and so forth.

09:54:08.600 --> 09:54:10.520
Now, once given a plot like this one,

09:54:10.520 --> 09:54:13.240
let's suppose we have a plot like this one.

09:54:13.240 --> 09:54:16.620
The aim here is to ask yourself the right question.

09:54:16.620 --> 09:54:20.180
If I want to make sure that my recall

09:54:20.180 --> 09:54:23.400
is always maximized, which is our case,

09:54:23.400 --> 09:54:26.320
we will try to ensure that we pick out

09:54:26.320 --> 09:54:28.960
these points around this.

09:54:28.960 --> 09:54:30.820
So we'll try to pick out these points

09:54:31.840 --> 09:54:32.920
towards the top right here.

09:54:32.920 --> 09:54:35.040
Let's take some of this off.

09:54:35.920 --> 09:54:40.520
So as we're saying, if we want to maximize our recall,

09:54:40.520 --> 09:54:43.980
is that normal that will pick out threshold values,

09:54:43.980 --> 09:54:46.160
which will take us around this region

09:54:46.160 --> 09:54:47.400
because it's around this region

09:54:47.400 --> 09:54:49.840
that our recall is maximized.

09:54:49.840 --> 09:54:52.460
Let's do this so you could see that clearer.

09:54:53.960 --> 09:54:58.080
Okay, now the problem with picking a point around this

09:54:58.080 --> 09:55:00.480
is that when you pick a point around this,

09:55:00.480 --> 09:55:03.320
the false positive rates is increased.

09:55:03.320 --> 09:55:06.020
So you need to find that balance

09:55:06.020 --> 09:55:09.500
between this false positive rate and true positive rate.

09:55:09.500 --> 09:55:12.720
So it will be much logical to pick a point

09:55:12.720 --> 09:55:14.560
around this right here.

09:55:14.560 --> 09:55:17.240
So we could pick around this region instead

09:55:18.580 --> 09:55:21.280
of this previous region right here.

09:55:21.280 --> 09:55:22.880
Now you could see that in this region,

09:55:22.880 --> 09:55:24.200
or let's say we pick this point.

09:55:24.200 --> 09:55:25.680
If you pick this point,

09:55:25.680 --> 09:55:28.680
your false positive rate now is smaller

09:55:28.680 --> 09:55:31.080
while your true positive rate is,

09:55:31.080 --> 09:55:33.720
or your recall is maximized,

09:55:33.720 --> 09:55:37.600
though it isn't the best possible recall we could have.

09:55:37.600 --> 09:55:41.480
But trying to focus on getting that recall of one

09:55:41.480 --> 09:55:44.520
will lead you into trouble since getting a recall of one

09:55:44.520 --> 09:55:48.880
in this case will increase our false positive rate.

09:55:48.880 --> 09:55:50.840
And then if we're dealing with a problem

09:55:50.840 --> 09:55:55.320
where we're trying to maximize the precision,

09:55:55.320 --> 09:55:56.680
then in that case,

09:55:56.680 --> 09:56:00.840
we want to ensure that this false positive rate is minimized.

09:56:00.840 --> 09:56:02.280
And so in this kind of problems,

09:56:02.280 --> 09:56:04.680
we'll want to pick a point around this.

09:56:04.680 --> 09:56:07.160
So you see, we want to pick this kind of value

09:56:07.160 --> 09:56:11.720
since at least our false positive rate is minimized.

09:56:11.720 --> 09:56:15.820
But then if you want to go and pick a point around this year,

09:56:15.820 --> 09:56:18.180
you would have a false positive rate of zero,

09:56:18.180 --> 09:56:22.760
but doing this will get you this into trouble

09:56:22.760 --> 09:56:25.600
because here you're going to have a true positive rate,

09:56:25.600 --> 09:56:27.120
which is very small.

09:56:27.120 --> 09:56:30.000
And so you need to get that balance.

09:56:30.000 --> 09:56:33.800
Now, if you're having a problem where it doesn't really matter

09:56:33.800 --> 09:56:35.760
that is you aren't trying to prioritize

09:56:35.760 --> 09:56:37.400
the precision or the recall

09:56:37.400 --> 09:56:40.120
and working with the accuracy is just fine,

09:56:40.120 --> 09:56:43.120
then you could pick out this point right here.

09:56:43.120 --> 09:56:46.400
So this is when you are having,

09:56:46.400 --> 09:56:48.600
or you don't have to prioritize on any,

09:56:48.600 --> 09:56:50.720
here is when you're trying to prioritize on the recall

09:56:50.720 --> 09:56:52.240
and here is when you're trying to prioritize

