10:50:33.240 --> 10:50:34.600
One, two, three.

10:50:34.600 --> 10:50:35.520
So that's fine.

10:50:35.520 --> 10:50:38.240
So notice that here we have this order.

10:50:38.240 --> 10:50:42.240
So we have the callbacks, learning rate scheduler.

10:50:42.240 --> 10:50:43.800
And we have CSV logger,

10:50:43.800 --> 10:50:47.000
LSTopping, learning rate scheduler under the callbacks.

10:50:47.000 --> 10:50:47.840
So that's fine.

10:50:48.720 --> 10:50:49.640
Let's get back to that.

10:50:49.640 --> 10:50:52.240
And then we are going to define.

10:50:52.240 --> 10:50:55.000
So here we've had the learning rate scheduler

10:50:55.000 --> 10:50:56.760
or this scheduler method,

10:50:56.760 --> 10:51:00.840
but we're yet to define our learning rate scheduler callback.

10:51:00.840 --> 10:51:05.840
So we have our, let's say scheduler.

10:51:05.960 --> 10:51:10.960
Scheduler callback equals learning rate scheduler.

10:51:11.760 --> 10:51:15.120
And then it takes in this scheduler method right here.

10:51:15.120 --> 10:51:16.000
So that's fine.

10:51:16.000 --> 10:51:19.920
Notice how the scheduler method takes in the current epoch

10:51:19.920 --> 10:51:23.360
and the current epoch number and the learning rate.

10:51:23.360 --> 10:51:26.840
So here we have this given to us already.

10:51:26.840 --> 10:51:31.640
And so we'll modify this to take, say for example, three.

10:51:31.640 --> 10:51:34.200
So after three epochs, we're going to modify the learning rate

10:51:34.200 --> 10:51:38.120
and then we could bring out the learning rate.

10:51:38.120 --> 10:51:42.400
So we could say, for example, the current learning,

10:51:42.400 --> 10:51:44.920
actually what we could do is let's take this off.

10:51:44.920 --> 10:51:46.360
Let's not have that.

10:51:46.360 --> 10:51:50.400
Let's specify the verbosity to be equal to one.

10:51:50.400 --> 10:51:54.080
So here we have the verbosity specified as one.

10:51:54.080 --> 10:51:59.000
And then we'll take off this.

10:51:59.000 --> 10:52:01.360
So you could also check out the CSV logger,

10:52:02.240 --> 10:52:05.180
the locked CSV file.

10:52:05.180 --> 10:52:09.000
So you'll notice how through our login these values

10:52:09.000 --> 10:52:12.600
since we just adding up or stacking up the values

10:52:12.600 --> 10:52:15.120
on the previous values we've had already.

10:52:15.120 --> 10:52:18.760
So for now, what we could do is take this off.

10:52:18.760 --> 10:52:22.680
Now let's take this off all this

10:52:22.680 --> 10:52:25.120
and then focus on just the scheduler.

10:52:25.120 --> 10:52:29.240
So we have scheduler callback and that's fine.

10:52:29.240 --> 10:52:32.120
Let's ensure that the cells have been around already.

