then there is a specialized print you could use.

14:29:38.580 --> 14:29:41.500
So yeah, instead of using the print,

14:29:41.500 --> 14:29:44.100
some sort of this print for the eager mode,

14:29:44.100 --> 14:29:47.780
the usual Python print, you could now use this print

14:29:47.780 --> 14:29:51.440
which is specially made for working in the graph mode.

14:29:51.440 --> 14:29:53.980
So here we have this print here

14:29:54.860 --> 14:29:57.220
and you see that the output of this tf.print

14:29:57.220 --> 14:29:58.860
is different from that of the print

14:29:58.860 --> 14:30:03.460
because now this tf.print makes this method

14:30:03.460 --> 14:30:06.860
look like a normal method as it goes through

14:30:06.860 --> 14:30:09.620
this print each and every time.

14:30:09.620 --> 14:30:11.980
Let's come in this and have this.

14:30:11.980 --> 14:30:13.300
So you see how this is printed.

