16:31:10.820 --> 16:31:15.820
was such that we have a multi-class problem.

16:31:15.820 --> 16:31:20.820
So even in the case where we have a binary classification problem

16:31:20.820 --> 16:31:25.820
like in this case, we expect to have an output of two values.

16:31:25.820 --> 16:31:28.820
So that's why when you have this output,

16:31:28.820 --> 16:31:31.820
let's get down here.

16:31:31.820 --> 16:31:33.820
Click on this.

16:31:33.820 --> 16:31:35.820
Let's add this code.

16:31:35.820 --> 16:31:38.820
So that's why when you have the value like say

16:31:38.820 --> 16:31:42.820
in the output 0.9,

16:31:42.820 --> 16:31:44.820
it's considered to be parasitized

16:31:44.820 --> 16:31:48.820
although we defined already that parasitized

16:31:48.820 --> 16:31:52.820
is meant to be zero, uninfected equal one.

16:31:52.820 --> 16:31:54.820
And so when we have 0.9,

16:31:54.820 --> 16:31:57.820
this is greater than the midpoint of this two,

16:31:57.820 --> 16:31:58.820
which is 0.5.

16:31:58.820 --> 16:32:01.820
So we should consider this as uninfected.

16:32:01.820 --> 16:32:02.820
But the way as we said already,

16:32:02.820 --> 16:32:05.820
the way this has been conceived is such that

16:32:05.820 --> 16:32:07.820
even in the binary classification problem,

16:32:07.820 --> 16:32:11.820
we shouldn't or we don't have a single output

16:32:11.820 --> 16:32:12.820
but two outputs.

16:32:12.820 --> 16:32:15.820
That is if we have a value of 0.9,

16:32:15.820 --> 16:32:19.820
what 1 dB expects to see is something like this,

16:32:19.820 --> 16:32:23.820
something like 0 and 0.9.

16:32:23.820 --> 16:32:25.820
So showing that here,

16:32:25.820 --> 16:32:27.820
let's even put here zero one,

16:32:27.820 --> 16:32:32.820
even 0.8 and 0.2.

16:32:32.820 --> 16:32:34.820
Okay, so let's have this.

16:32:34.820 --> 16:32:35.820
So even in this case,

16:32:35.820 --> 16:32:38.820
it goes back to the same output.

16:32:38.820 --> 16:32:43.820
So this simply means that we are having

16:32:43.820 --> 16:32:46.820
an uninfected cell since this first index here

16:32:46.820 --> 16:32:49.820
has a higher value.

16:32:49.820 --> 16:32:50.820
Now to solve this issue,

16:32:50.820 --> 16:32:52.820
what we're going to do is,

16:32:52.820 --> 16:32:54.820
we're going to take each and every output we have

16:32:54.820 --> 16:32:56.820
and convert it to this format.

16:32:56.820 --> 16:32:58.820
So in the case where we have, for example,

16:32:58.820 --> 16:33:00.820
0.1 as output,

16:33:00.820 --> 16:33:03.820
we're going to convert it into 1, 0

16:33:03.820 --> 16:33:07.820
because this means that the higher,

16:33:07.820 --> 16:33:10.820
this one means that it's parasitized cell

16:33:10.820 --> 16:33:12.820
and this two means the same

16:33:12.820 --> 16:33:15.820
because here we're seeing that this zeroth index,

16:33:15.820 --> 16:33:18.820
which is the parasitized index,

16:33:18.820 --> 16:33:20.820
has a higher value.

16:33:20.820 --> 16:33:24.820
Hence, this is a parasitized cell.

16:33:24.820 --> 16:33:26.820
So that said, what we're going to do now is,

16:33:26.820 --> 16:33:29.820
for all values less than 0.5,

16:33:29.820 --> 16:33:31.820
we could say less than, yeah, 0.5,

16:33:31.820 --> 16:33:34.820
we are going to convert it into 0,

16:33:34.820 --> 16:33:37.820
sorry, we're going to convert it into 1, 0.

16:33:37.820 --> 16:33:40.820
And then for all values greater than 0.5,

16:33:40.820 --> 16:33:44.820
we're going to convert them into 0, 1.

16:33:44.820 --> 16:33:47.820
So this is the transformation we're going to make

16:33:47.820 --> 16:33:50.820
in order for this 1DB log method

16:33:50.820 --> 16:33:53.820
to correctly log our values.

16:33:53.820 --> 16:33:57.820
